# Pull request reviews

When the user asks to review a pull request, comment on the PR first, then summarize in chat.

1. Post the review on the pull request.
   - Put each finding as an inline comment on the line it refers to.
   - Add a short summary review comment.
   - If there are no findings, post that summary anyway.
2. After those comments are on the pull request, summarize the same findings in the chat.
   - Lead with the findings.
   - Include the review link.

Do not finish a review in chat only.

```markdown
# Review order

1. https://github.com/org/repo/pull/1#pullrequestreview-… (inline comments posted)
2. Chat summary of the same findings, with that link
```
